{
  "id": "COMPOUND:37978 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Flemichapparin is shown to interact with Cyclin-dependent kinase 1/cyclin B, which is a well-documented target of the compound. This kinase complex is known to regulate cell cycle progression and is a key player in various cellular processes, including proliferation and survival. The evidence suggests that Flemichapparin acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Isodomoic acid A and 1,4,5,6-Tetrahydroxy-2-(2-methylbut-3-en-2-yl)xanthen-9-one, all of which ultimately target Neuropilin-2. This indicates a potential pathway where Flemichapparin may modulate the activity of these kinases, which in turn influence Neuropilin-2 function. The consistent interaction across different compounds supports a mechanistic link between Flemichapparin and Neuropilin-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a strong, though not entirely conclusive, relationship, which would require further experimental validation to confirm the therapeutic relevance.",
